# Act 1, level 2: the outer wall to the castle gate (G2, grey-box). Folds in
# the wall, the bailey and the gate rooms as sections. The climb up the outer
# wall's three storeys with bats round the ladders; a skeleton asleep on the
# walk; the gatehouse, whose sill is where a throw lands on top of the guard
# (the outer wall's lesson); the breach over spikes on slabs that fall. A high
# road up the gatehouse tower crosses the breach on scaffolds instead, past two
# bats. Then the bailey: wood holds a sword and stone does not, the caged
# dragon over a quiet stretch, a yard whose switch raises the gate ahead. Then
# the ditch, crossed by standing on your own sword under a bat, and the gate
# yard: the castle stands on a plinth whose face is the switch, and its gate
# ends the act. Castle tiles until it plays (Matt, 2026-10-07).
size 16
[map]
